From 7de366486923ee06d80669086cf6e7b85418ce45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericman2001 <ericman2001@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:35:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/17] arm64: dts: qcom: Add HP Googlebook (Quartz)

Add initial support for the HP Googlebook "Quartz" (Google Bluey
baseboard) with the Snapdragon X Elite (X1E80100).

The firmware is coreboot + depthcharge, which enters Linux at EL2 and
applies the dtbo partition's overlays onto this DT, so:

 - the Gunyah-specific parts of hamoa.dtsi are adjusted as in x1-el2.dtso
   (apss watchdog enabled, SBSA watchdog disabled),
 - the GIC ITS is disabled, as in the stock DTB,
 - reserved-memory follows the stock vendor DTB,
 - the DTB is built with symbols.

GPIOs 34-35 and 44-47 belong to the secure world; touching them raises a
NoC error that QTEE treats as fatal.

The display is the coreboot-initialised eDP framebuffer for now. MDSS is
enabled without a driver bound so that the interconnect providers keep the
firmware's bandwidth votes for it.

The Chrome EC (keyboard included, with its Fn layer) is on QUP SE13 SPI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
